Falsifies `file_allocation_table::long_name::verification::every_alias_reads_back_through_its_tail_number`.

The defect: the tail is read from the first `~` of the base rather than the last, so the alias of a
name that carries its own `~`, such as `a~b.txt`, reads as no number at all. The writer then never
sees that alias taken, and two names in one directory share it.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(tail_number(&alias), Some(number))`.

